{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>When you go out as a camp.</b> This is the camp that goes out against the enemy, and there the Ark is. It is the small camp, not the great camp, for there partitions are made. When they go out to war, they are stationed around the Ark. It is clear that impurity comes by occurrence of destruction. This section follows because of the war against Midian, for he mentioned the matter of Balaam, for they are enemies because of their sister. And the Ark was with the camp that went out against Midian." "<b>From every evil thing.</b> For soul and body, like the emission [קרי]."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "The phrase 'because of their sister' (בעבור אחותם) is textually difficult in context; translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:24:28.151688132Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}